title: Grid pushing
intro: Sokoban crates with no code: a grid player pushes them a cell at a time, onto goals that count when they're covered.
project: Empty | Crate Push

chapter: A room with crates | A crate on a grid, and a goal
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 11111111\n1......1\n1.11...1\n1......1\n11111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 4
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
look: 4, -2.5, 4
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position.X = 1.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
say: A small room on a tilemap, and a grid player in its top left corner.
deselect
create: Crate
rename: Crate A
set: Transform.Position.X = 3.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
explain: component:GridMovement | A grid crate | A crate made in a scene with a grid player is a grid crate: a Pushable with a Grid Movement of its own, and no gravity.
explain: group:Pushable.Grid | Pushes Row and Kind | Pushes Row lets it shove the crates behind it along too. Off, as in Sokoban, a crate behind it blocks the push. Kind is for goals that only take some crates.
deselect
create: Crate
rename: Crate B
set: Transform.Position.X = 2.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -3.5
deselect
create: Goal
rename: Goal A
set: Transform.Position.X = 5.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
explain: menu:Entity | Entity, Genres, Puzzles, Goal | Goal, under Puzzles, makes a place to push a crate to: a flat square drawn under the crates.
explain: component:Goal | Goal | It's covered while a crate rests in its cell. The crate turns its Covered Tint, and it can play a sound and send messages.
explain: field:Goal.AllCoveredMessage | All Covered Message | Every goal with the same All Covered Message sends it once they're all covered: the level solved.
deselect
create: Goal
rename: Goal B
set: Transform.Position.X = 4.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -3.5
deselect
create: Text
rename: Crates
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Anchor = TopLeft
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 2.5, -0.7
add: Counter
set: Counter.Track = *
set: Counter.Output = Goals Covered
set: Counter.Format = Crates: {0} / {2}
explain: field:Counter.Output | Goals Covered | And a counter that counts the covered goals, an output, instead of a message, with how many there are, for the corner of the screen.

chapter: Push them home | One cell a step, stopped by walls
play
wait: 0.5
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
expectat: Crate A = 4.5, -1.5
say: Step into a crate and it slides a cell ahead, gliding along with the player.
tap: Right
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate A = 5.5, -1.5
expectvalue: Crates.Text.Value = Crates: 1 / 2
explain: game | Covered | On its goal it turns green, and the counter goes up.
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
tap: Down
wait: 0.3
tap: Down
wait: 0.3
say: Round the wall in the middle, to get behind the other crate.
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
tap: Right
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate B = 4.5, -3.5
expectvalue: Crates.Text.Value = Crates: 2 / 2
explain: game | Solved | Both goals are covered, so they send Solved, once. A sound player or a script can hear it and move on to the next level.
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
tap: Right
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate B = 6.5, -3.5
expectat: Player = 5.5, -3.5
explain: game | Off again | Push a crate off its goal and the count goes down. Against the wall it won't go any further, so the player just bumps it.
stop
say: That's grid pushing, with no code. It works with turns too, where a push is the player's step, and in network games.
